WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.362
Run this query and compare several truncated
versions of each order timestamp The

00:00:06.375 --> 00:00:12.129
original timestamp keeps the precise event time The
day version maps

00:00:12.155 --> 00:00:17.109
it to the start of the day The month version maps it
to the start

00:00:17.123 --> 00:00:22.436
of the month This is how a precise event can be
analyzed at a coarser

00:00:22.449 --> 00:00:25.225
reporting grain without changing the stored source
value
